    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Before proceeding further, it may be helpful to summarize the assumptions that we are making:\n\n• The organism is diploid.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b4",
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b5"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          299.0,
          895.0,
          1052.0,
          948.0
        ],
        [
          326.0,
          965.0,
          585.0,
          987.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 0.474227,
      "content_sha256": "52cac40cb391b17c1df1a68b2f69f7a9f0d798edbffb2495eec6a28b800ed066",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Reproduction is sexual.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b6"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          326.0,
          993.0,
          577.0,
          1013.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "2ede0d66754b5c7ecaf571f8686fc532272b11037830db04dad3d59dd65e3b33",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Generations are nonoverlapping.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b7"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          326.0,
          1019.0,
          671.0,
          1041.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "1948417ba869c106729cc3404ab474a8bcdd9906b56b05ee9ed8da8d33498f0f",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• The gene under consideration has two alleles.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b8"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          326.0,
          1043.0,
          797.0,
          1066.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "1bb88c53934e1f38125348e3ad3138d01d8ba48432789d89573d711335e9111f",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• The allele frequencies are identical in males and females.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b9"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          326.0,
          1068.0,
          902.0,
          1092.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "89bd7d6ea7d40e57db3f99f7d362ec1c17487b6fe03c5d7d2ba971d6866a4def",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Mating is random.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b10"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          327.0,
          1100.0,
          530.0,
          1120.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "917d91601241bbd2bf1d527d903be02c92bfd2ecd3122200c2188aabe577c502",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Population size is very large (in theory, infinite).",
      "source_page": 66,
      "source_pages": [
        66
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p008:b6"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          281.0,
          785.0,
          1035.0,
          1264.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 0.756098,
      "content_sha256": "3dfd5aa637fe12be67aa91477b789c3be39f997dcb8270ea66447b563e269e4b",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Migration is negligible.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b12"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          328.0,
          1153.0,
          577.0,
          1176.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "b7d8986ab9b1b6afe01a841a2a9b638c5da89ac6da218aaad000b70e64ec19d0",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Mutation can be ignored.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b13"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          328.0,
          1179.0,
          595.0,
          1200.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "499bc144b2fb7f0b0664e890c32ca598a16e4951e5cb004d66ce8d41f372720c",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "• Natural selection does not affect the alleles under consideration.",
      "source_page": 99,
      "source_pages": [
        99
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p041:b3",
        "PopGen_chapter2:p041:b4"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          105.0,
          652.0,
          857.0,
          809.0
        ],
        [
          103.0,
          812.0,
          855.0,
          944.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 0.719298,
      "content_sha256": "75bf75148acd04363e47fcee5cb39ca235ffdfab41fd086ff703132006468048",
      "source_locator_mode": "matched",
      "inline_styles": []
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Collectively, these assumptions summarize the Hardy-Weinberg model, named after the English mathematician G. H. Hardy (1877–1947) and the German physiologist Wilhelm Weinberg (1862–1937), who, in 1908, independently formulated the model and deduced its theoretical predictions of genotype frequency.",
      "source_page": 62,
      "source_pages": [
        62
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b15"
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          304.0,
          1241.0,
          1057.0,
          1378.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "a4d8b04581e154877fadb13071926f3daacb0afd07e859299243be650f399113",
      "inline_styles": [
        {
          "start": 46,
          "end": 66,
          "style": "italic",
          "text": "Hardy-Weinberg model",
          "source_page": 62,
          "source_block_ids": [
            "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b15"
          ],
          "source_bboxes": [
            [
              304.0,
              1241.0,
              1057.0,
              1378.0
            ]
          ],
          "source_content_sha256": "aa0112d1cc79a45e00c45ba3932cfd0ad39a66902a5caf201d827a902529489b",
          "subject_index": null,
          "source_content_hashes": {
            "PopGen_chapter2:p004:b15": "aa0112d1cc79a45e00c45ba3932cfd0ad39a66902a5caf201d827a902529489b"
          }
        }
      ],
      "source_locator_mode": "matched"
