    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In the Hardy-Weinberg model, the mathematical relation between the allele frequencies and the genotype frequencies is given by $$ AA:p^{2}\\qquad Aa:2pq\\qquad aa:q^{2} $$ in which $ p^{2} $, $ 2pq $, and $ q^{2} $ are the frequencies of the genotypes AA, Aa, and aa in zygotes of any generation, p and q are the allele frequencies of A and a in gametes of the previous generation, and $ p + q = 1 $. The frequencies displayed in Equation 2.1 constitute the Hardy-Weinberg principle or the Hardy-Weinberg equilibrium (HWE).",
      "source_page": 63,
      "source_pages": [
        63
      ],
      "source_block_ids": [
        "PopGen_chapter2:p005:b1",
        "PopGen_chapter2:p005:b2",
        "PopGen_chapter2:p005:b3"
